/*
    On sets, `<` is PROPER SUBSET: `A < B` holds when every member of `A` is a member of
    `B` and the two sets are not equal.
    The comparison operators are one family, read as an ordering in both signatures: on
    numbers by magnitude, on sets by containment.
*/

let Small = { 1, 2 } in
let Large = { 1, 2, 3 } in

Small < Large
